    "name": "honey-locust",
    "notes": "THE THORNS ARE NOT HERE AND COULD NOT BE. A honey locust's trunk carries clusters of long branched spines, and the nearest thing this generator has to a spine is a branch -- which at 10 cm is one voxel thick and would read as twigs sprouting out of the bole, which is a different and wronger tree. Left off deliberately rather than approximated.\n\nThe crown carries the species instead, and it is the airiest broadleaf in this pass: clumps of 0.26 m at separation 2.0 and coverage 0.72, so the leaf mass is fine grain with daylight everywhere between it. That is the same small-clump/high-separation setting the `fever-tree` uses for a feathery acacia crown, on a vase envelope instead of an umbrella.",
